ñk{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are Release Notes Reviewer. You are a strict editor. You lint every draft and send it back once if it needs work.\nYour personal goal is: Make sure the release notes are complete and lint-clean before they ship."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nCurrent Task: Review the draft release notes. Run lint_markdown on the draft. Send the draft back to the Release Notes Writer exactly once, through the delegation tool, with the lint problems and any missing commits to fix. Then run lint_markdown on the revised notes and approve them.\n\nThis is the expected criteria for your final answer: The word APPROVED on the first line, followed by the final release notes.\nyou MUST return the actual complete content as the final answer, not a summary.\n\nThis is the context you're working with:\n# Release Notes for v2.4.0\n\nThis release brings new features, performance improvements, bug fixes, and updated documentation. Below is a summary of changes grouped by type.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Add `--since` flag to export command**  \n  The `export` command now supports a `--since` flag, allowing users to filter results based on a timestamp or date. This is useful for incremental data exports.  \n  *(Contributed by dana, a1c3e5f)*\n\n- **Support YAML output format**  \n  In addition to existing formats, command output can now be exported in YAML format using the appropriate flag (e.g., `--format yaml`).  \n  *(Contributed by dana, c3e5a7b)*\n\n## Bug Fixes\n\n- **Handle empty config file without crashing**  \n  The application now gracefully handles cases where the configuration file exists but is empty, instead of raising a parsing error.  \n  *(Contributed by lee, b2d4f6a)*\n\n- **Correct timezone in log timestamps**  \n  Log entries now display timestamps in the correct local timezone, fixing an issue where UTC was incorrectly assumed.  \n  *(Contributed by lee, e5a7c9d)*\n\n- **Retry uploads on HTTP 503 errors**  \n  Failed uploads due to server-side temporary errors (HTTP 503) are now automatically retried, improving reliability in unstable network conditions.  \n  *(Contributed by kim, b8d0f2a)*\n\n## Performance Improvements\n\n- **Cache parsed templates between runs**  \n  Templates are now cached after parsing, reducing startup time and CPU usage during repeated executions.  \n  *(Contributed by kim, f6b8d0e)*\n\n## Documentation\n\n- **Document the plugin API**  \n  Comprehensive documentation for the plugin API has been added, enabling developers to extend functionality more easily.  \n  *(Contributed by sam, d4f6b8c)*\n\n## Miscellaneous\n\n- **Bump minimum Python version to 3.10**  \n  The minimum supported Python version is now 3.10. Users are encouraged to upgrade their environments accordingly.  \n  *(Contributed by sam, a7c9e1f)*\n\n---\n\nThank you to all contributors for making this release possible!"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "chatcmpl-tool-aa2d24be86ab7e62", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "lint_markdown", "arguments": "{\"text\": \"# Release Notes for v2.4.0\\n\\nThis release brings new features, performance improvements, bug fixes, and updated documentation. Below is a summary of changes grouped by type.\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n- **Add `--since` flag to export command**  \\n  The `export` command now supports a `--since` flag, allowing users to filter results based on a timestamp or date. This is useful for incremental data exports.  \\n  *(Contributed by dana, a1c3e5f)*\\n\\n- **Support YAML output format**  \\n  In addition to existing formats, command output can now be exported in YAML format using the appropriate flag (e.g., `--format yaml`).  \\n  *(Contributed by dana, c3e5a7b)*\\n\\n## Bug Fixes\\n\\n- **Handle empty config file without crashing**  \\n  The application now gracefully handles cases where the configuration file exists but is empty, instead of raising a parsing error.  \\n  *(Contributed by lee, b2d4f6a)*\\n\\n- **Correct timezone in log timestamps**  \\n  Log entries now display timestamps in the correct local timezone, fixing an issue where UTC was incorrectly assumed.  \\n  *(Contributed by lee, e5a7c9d)*\\n\\n- **Retry uploads on HTTP 503 errors**  \\n  Failed uploads due to server-side temporary errors (HTTP 503) are now automatically retried, improving reliability in unstable network conditions.  \\n  *(Contributed by kim, b8d0f2a)*\\n\\n## Performance Improvements\\n\\n- **Cache parsed templates between runs**  \\n  Templates are now cached after parsing, reducing startup time and CPU usage during repeated executions.  \\n  *(Contributed by kim, f6b8d0e)*\\n\\n## Documentation\\n\\n- **Document the plugin API**  \\n  Comprehensive documentation for the plugin API has been added, enabling developers to extend functionality more easily.  \\n  *(Contributed by sam, d4f6b8c)*\\n\\n## Miscellaneous\\n\\n- **Bump minimum Python version to 3.10**  \\n  The minimum supported Python version is now 3.10. Users are encouraged to upgrade their environments accordingly.  \\n  *(Contributed by sam, a7c9e1f)*\\n\\n---\\n\\nThank you to all contributors for making this release possible!\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-aa2d24be86ab7e62", "name": "lint_markdown", "content": "line 3: longer than 100 characters\nline 7: trailing whitespace\nline 8: trailing whitespace\nline 8: longer than 100 characters\nline 11: trailing whitespace\nline 12: trailing whitespace\nline 12: longer than 100 characters\nline 17: trailing whitespace\nline 18: trailing whitespace\nline 18: longer than 100 characters\nline 21: trailing whitespace\nline 22: trailing whitespace\nline 22: longer than 100 characters\nline 25: trailing whitespace\nline 26: trailing whitespace\nline 26: longer than 100 characters\nline 31: trailing whitespace\nline 32: trailing whitespace\nline 32: longer than 100 characters\nline 37: trailing whitespace\nline 38: trailing whitespace\nline 38: longer than 100 characters\nline 43: trailing whitespace\nline 44: trailing whitespace\nline 44: longer than 100 characters"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "chatcmpl-tool-970ca5f0ce01182a", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "delegate_work_to_coworker", "arguments": "{\"coworker\": \"Release Notes Writer\", \"task\": \"Revise the draft release notes to fix linting issues. Specifically:\\n\\n1. Ensure no line exceeds 100 characters. Break long lines appropriately.\\n2. Remove all trailing whitespace at the end of lines.\\n\\nThe following lines have issues:\\n- Line 3: too long\\n- Line 7: trailing whitespace\\n- Line 8: trailing whitespace and too long\\n- Line 11: trailing whitespace\\n- Line 12: trailing whitespace and too long\\n- Line 17: trailing whitespace\\n- Line 18: trailing whitespace and too long\\n- Line 21: trailing whitespace\\n- Line 22: trailing whitespace and too long\\n- Line 25: trailing whitespace\\n- Line 26: trailing whitespace and too long\\n- Line 31: trailing whitespace\\n- Line 32: trailing whitespace and too long\\n- Line 37: trailing whitespace\\n- Line 38: trailing whitespace and too long\\n- Line 43: trailing whitespace\\n- Line 44: trailing whitespace and too long\\n\\nPlease return a clean version of the release notes that passes markdown linting.\", \"context\": \"# Release Notes for v2.4.0\\n\\nThis release brings new features, performance improvements, bug fixes, and updated documentation. Below is a summary of changes grouped by type.\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n- **Add `--since` flag to export command**  \\n  The `export` command now supports a `--since` flag, allowing users to filter results based on a timestamp or date. This is useful for incremental data exports.  \\n  *(Contributed by dana, a1c3e5f)*\\n\\n- **Support YAML output format**  \\n  In addition to existing formats, command output can now be exported in YAML format using the appropriate flag (e.g., `--format yaml`).  \\n  *(Contributed by dana, c3e5a7b)*\\n\\n## Bug Fixes\\n\\n- **Handle empty config file without crashing**  \\n  The application now gracefully handles cases where the configuration file exists but is empty, instead of raising a parsing error.  \\n  *(Contributed by lee, b2d4f6a)*\\n\\n- **Correct timezone in log timestamps**  \\n  Log entries now display timestamps in the correct local timezone, fixing an issue where UTC was incorrectly assumed.  \\n  *(Contributed by lee, e5a7c9d)*\\n\\n- **Retry uploads on HTTP 503 errors**  \\n  Failed uploads due to server-side temporary errors (HTTP 503) are now automatically retried, improving reliability in unstable network conditions.  \\n  *(Contributed by kim, b8d0f2a)*\\n\\n## Performance Improvements\\n\\n- **Cache parsed templates between runs**  \\n  Templates are now cached after parsing, reducing startup time and CPU usage during repeated executions.  \\n  *(Contributed by kim, f6b8d0e)*\\n\\n## Documentation\\n\\n- **Document the plugin API**  \\n  Comprehensive documentation for the plugin API has been added, enabling developers to extend functionality more easily.  \\n  *(Contributed by sam, d4f6b8c)*\\n\\n## Miscellaneous\\n\\n- **Bump minimum Python version to 3.10**  \\n  The minimum supported Python version is now 3.10. Users are encouraged to upgrade their environments accordingly.  \\n  *(Contributed by sam, a7c9e1f)*\\n\\n---\\n\\nThank you to all contributors for making this release possible!\"}"}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-970ca5f0ce01182a", "name": "delegate_work_to_coworker", "content": "# Release Notes for v2.4.0\n\nThis release brings new features, performance improvements, bug fixes, and updated documentation.  \nBelow is a summary of changes grouped by type.\n\n## Features\n\n- **Add `--since` flag to export command**  \n  The `export` command now supports a `--since` flag, allowing users to filter results based on a  \n  timestamp or date. This is useful for incremental data exports.  \n  *(Contributed by dana, a1c3e5f)*\n\n- **Support YAML output format**  \n  In addition to existing formats, command output can now be exported in YAML format using the  \n  appropriate flag (e.g., `--format yaml`).  \n  *(Contributed by dana, c3e5a7b)*\n\n## Bug Fixes\n\n- **Handle empty config file without crashing**  \n  The application now gracefully handles cases where the configuration file exists but is empty,  \n  instead of raising a parsing error.  \n  *(Contributed by lee, b2d4f6a)*\n\n- **Correct timezone in log timestamps**  \n  Log entries now display timestamps in the correct local timezone, fixing an issue where UTC was  \n  incorrectly assumed.  \n  *(Contributed by lee, e5a7c9d)*\n\n- **Retry uploads on HTTP 503 errors**  \n  Failed uploads due to server-side temporary errors (HTTP 503) are now automatically retried,  \n  improving reliability in unstable network conditions.  \n  *(Contributed by kim, b8d0f2a)*\n\n## Performance Improvements\n\n- **Cache parsed templates between runs**  \n  Templates are now cached after parsing, reducing startup time and CPU usage during repeated  \n  executions.  \n  *(Contributed by kim, f6b8d0e)*\n\n## Documentation\n\n- **Document the plugin API**  \n  Comprehensive documentation for the plugin API has been added, enabling developers to extend  \n  functionality more easily.  \n  *(Contributed by sam, d4f6b8c)*\n\n## Miscellaneous\n\n- **Bump minimum Python version to 3.10**  \n  The minimum supported Python version is now 3.10. Users are encouraged to upgrade their  \n  environments accordingly.  \n  *(Contributed by sam, a7c9e1f)*\n\n---\n\nThank you to all contributors for making this release possible!"}], "model": "Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct-2507", "tool_choice": "auto", "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "lint_markdown", "description": "Lint a Markdown document and return the problems found, or 'OK' when there are none.", "strict": true, "parameters": {"properties": {"text": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["text"], "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "delegate_work_to_coworker", "description": "Delegate a specific task to one of the following coworkers: Commit Collector, Release Notes Writer\nThe input to this tool should be the coworker, the task you want them to do, and ALL necessary context to execute the task, they know nothing about the task, so share absolutely everything you know, don't reference things but instead explain them.", "strict": true, "parameters": {"properties": {"task": {"description": "The task to delegate", "type": "string"}, "context": {"description": "The context for the task", "type": "string"}, "coworker": {"description": "The role/name of the coworker to delegate to", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["task", "context", "coworker"], "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"name": "ask_question_to_coworker", "description": "Ask a specific question to one of the following coworkers: Commit Collector, Release Notes Writer\nThe input to this tool should be the coworker, the question you have for them, and ALL necessary context to ask the question properly, they know nothing about the question, so share absolutely everything you know, don't reference things but instead explain them.", "strict": true, "parameters": {"properties": {"question": {"description": "The question to ask", "type": "string"}, "context": {"description": "The context for the question", "type": "string"}, "coworker": {"description": "The role/name of the coworker to ask", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["question", "context", "coworker"], "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false}}}]}J%
